  "selection_id": "LIVENESS-PREFLIGHT-24",
  "owner": "lead",
  "frozen": "2026-09-09",
  "purpose": "Measure the effective-support distribution under thinking OFF, which no existing data reports, and test whether OFF moves support in the SAME DIRECTION for GPT and Claude. A differential ON->OFF effect by model family sits directly on top of the cross-family similarity measure and would matter more than the identifiability question.",
  "design": "Within-array, within-checkpoint ON->OFF contrast. The two checkpoints are the only two with existing four-option data on every B203 array, so every OFF cell has a paired ON cell at the same n on the same images and the same prompt d40ea45d. The ONLY difference is the request surface.",
  "checkpoints": [
    "gpt-5.5-2026-04-23",
    "claude-opus-5"
  ],
  "n_per_cell": 24,
  "n_arrays": 24,
  "n_calls": 1152,
  "selection_rule": "Rank all 203 B203 arrays by min(eff_support_gpt, eff_support_opus5) measured under adaptive-ON at n=24. Three strata by fixed cut points on that value: high >= 1.60, mid 1.10-1.59, low < 1.10. Take 8 per stratum, round-robin over families by rank so distinct families are maximised. Deterministic, no RNG.",
  "conditioning_disclosure": "This selection conditions on a WITHIN-MODEL marginal (how deterministic each model is on the array), measured on two checkpoints that are themselves in the panel. It does NOT condition on any BETWEEN-model relationship - not on agreement, not on cross-model match, not on modal coincidence. That is a weaker form of selection than the one that disqualified FROZEN_22, whose rule was literally \"GPT-5.5 share >= .75 and FC >= .80\". It is weaker, not absent, and it is declared: results from the liveness-screened stratum are reported as conditioned on a generator property, never as a property of the battery.",
  "not_a_frame_screen": "This preflight does NOT reduce VIS-FRAME-41. The full 41-array frame is collected as approved. The preflight defines a DECLARED STRATUM within it plus the extra live arrays, and prevalence of collapse is reported on the full unscreened frame as a substantive result.",
